 ## Release authoring contract
 
 See the [complete authoring and delivery contract](../../plans/theme-api-authoring-contract.md) for typed/managed layers, portable companion recipes, pressed presentation, family refinements, consumed-role provenance, rendered alpha validation and licensed font delivery. `fontStyle` is a bounded normal/italic/oblique token type. Opt into unknown library-hook diagnostics with `resolveTheme({warnUnknownComponentHooks:true})`.
+
+### Scoped companion typography
+
+Code-authored `ThemeCompanionRecipe` rules can target `button`, `card`, `field`, `badge`, `tab` and `choice` families. In addition to connected typed override hooks, they can assign registered public `font.ui`, `font.input`, `font.metadata`, `font.body` and `font.label-strong` roles (including absolute small/medium/large size outputs). Values must reference compatible typed tokens; arbitrary CSS, unknown properties and mechanical inputs are rejected. Rules retain the enclosing theme/appearance boundary and exclude descendant theme boundaries.
+
+Button variants remain `primary`, `secondary`, `ghost`, `danger`. Badge variants are `neutral`, `accent`, `success`, `warning`, `danger`. Theme-wide normal typography can therefore stay regular while scoped action typography stays medium and badge typography becomes compact. A theme author must declare typed source entries for optional public hooks that are registered but absent from the default source document. Export the generated companion alongside the theme CSS; changing only the global token CSS does not deliver scoped recipes.
+
+Code-owned companion rules also support finite `presentation` recipes: `joined` for `segmented-control`, `dotted-underline` for `link`, and `stretch` for `standalone-action`. These emit scoped CSS over public Parts/native classes, rather than reading layout from computed styles or accepting imported CSS. They are regenerated from the canonical recipe on import. Joined groups retain native radio semantics and targets, visible focus, disabled behavior, logical corners and forced colors.
+
+`reset-action` and `standalone-action` target buttons explicitly annotated with `data-en-action="reset"` and `data-en-action="standalone"`, respectively. These are optional styling roles, not behavior or ARIA roles. A reset recipe can supply neutral outlined paint without changing every ghost button. The standalone stretch recipe sizes both the custom-element host and its `control` Part; consumers annotate only the form/card actions whose allocation should fill the available width. Unannotated toolbar/header/icon actions remain content-sized. Layout owners can also directly set host and `::part(control)` inline size with CSS. Use `en-link` or a native `.en-link` with `links.css` to opt into link styling.
